---
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n";
import { visits } from "../../config/booking";
import { legalSlugs, owner } from "../../config/legal";

const privacy = getRelativeLocaleUrl("en", legalSlugs[1]);
const mail = `mailto:${owner.email}`;
const euro = new Intl.NumberFormat("en", {
  style: "currency",
  currency: "EUR",
  maximumFractionDigits: 0,
});
---

<p>
  Here is, in a few lines, what each visit costs, how to pay and what happens if
  you need to change or cancel your appointment.
</p>

<h2>Prices and what each visit includes</h2>
<p>
  Visits are always by video call. Prices include VAT and you receive an invoice
  for each visit.
</p>
<div class="block">
  <h3>First visit: {euro.format(visits.first.price)}</h3>
  <p>
    We draw your family tree together, answer your questions and agree on a
    plan. It lasts about 60 minutes. It can run longer or shorter depending on
    your case and, if it runs longer, it costs no more.
  </p>
</div>
<div class="block">
  <h3>Follow-up: {euro.format(visits.followup.price)}</h3>
  <p>
    To pick the plan back up and answer the questions that come up after the
    first visit.
  </p>
</div>
<p>
  After every visit you receive a written report with the points we covered and
  the genetic counselling assessment.
</p>

<h2>If you need genetic testing</h2>
<p>
  If we see that genetic testing makes sense in your case, we will recommend it.
  The test is carried out by an independent laboratory (mainly Health in Code),
  which invoices you and charges you directly, after you sign the informed
  consent with it. We do not collect or handle that payment and we receive no
  commission. The price of the visit does not include the test. If there is a
  test, you also receive the laboratory's result and our assessment.
</p>

<h2>How to pay</h2>
<p>
  The price of the visit is paid when you book, online, with Stripe. The
  appointment is confirmed once the payment is complete. We never see your full
  card details. More information in the <a href={privacy}>privacy policy</a>.
</p>

<h2>Changing the date or cancelling</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Up to 48 hours before the appointment:</strong> you can change the
    date or cancel at no cost and we refund 100 % of what you paid.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Less than 48 hours before, or if you don't connect:</strong> no
    refund.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>
      If we cancel, or the video call can't take place because of a technical
      failure on our side:
    </strong>{" "}
    you choose between a new date or 100 % of the amount.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  To change or cancel, use the link in the confirmation email or write to{" "}
  <a href={mail}>{owner.email}</a>.
</p>

<h2>How we refund you</h2>
<p>
  The refund goes back to the same payment method you used. We process it within
  5 working days at most. After that, your bank may take a few more days to show
  it.
</p>

<h2>Right of withdrawal</h2>
<p>
  When you buy at a distance you have the right to withdraw, without giving a
  reason, within 14 calendar days of booking. To do so, write to{" "}
  <a href={mail}>{owner.email}</a> and tell us you withdraw.
</p>
<p>
  There is one exception. If you ask us to hold the consultation before those 14
  days are over, for example by booking a date within that period, and the
  consultation takes place in full, you can no longer withdraw, because the
  service has been provided. When you book, we will ask you to confirm that you
  want the consultation to start within the period.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
  If you have any questions about these terms, write to{" "}
  <a href={mail}>{owner.email}</a>.
</p>

<p>
  This text is a translation of the Spanish original. If the two differ, the
  Spanish terms prevail.
</p>
